text smt110 "below"
text smt111 "cuda-map"
text smt112 "Each piece of CUDA and Omega's replacement"
text smt113 "<p>CUDA is a stack of NVIDIA software. Each piece is shown from the top of the stack to the chip. Missing pieces are shown as missing. PASS means a receipt exists on the named commit; PARTIAL, MISSING and NOT REPLACEABLE remain separate.</p>"
text smt114 "today"
text smt115 "What is already true, with a receipt"
text smt116 "<p>The receipt holds the binary sha256, mapped libraries, ldd, driver version and commands used.</p></section>"
text smt117 "not-yet"
text smt118 "What is not true yet"
text smt119 "not_yet"
text smt120 "The bar for Omega replaces CUDA: C1 to C6"
text smt121 "<p>I say it when every row is PASS, each with a receipt pushed on the exact commit. No row is waived. A row is ticked here only when its receipt is in the data file.</p>"
text smt122 "beyond"
text smt123 "Beyond the CUDA claim"
text smt124 "<p>These are not part of the CUDA claim. They are the rest of what Omega is for, and each has its own bar.</p>"
