text smt160 "The bodies of one machine"
text smt161 "machines"
text smt162 "Five machines, one project"
text smt163 "<p>A DGX Spark, an Intel iMac, a Raspberry Pi 5, QEMU and a Windows PC target. QEMU is an emulator, not a physical body. AienOS is the operating-system project; Aienux is its kernel. These are dated inventory observations, not live telemetry.</p><p>Inventory as of "
text smt164 "as_of"
text smt165 ". Each card states its environment, evidence date, branch and limitations.</p><div class=\"dashboard-grid\">"
text smt166 "<div id=\"machine-"
text smt167 "</div><p><a href=\"/classic/#speed\">The speeds measured on them, with receipts</a> · <a href=\"/machines.json\">The inventory data</a></p></section>"
text smt168 "speed"
text smt169 "Speed, with receipts"
text smt170 "<p>Recorded model and engine runs, not a claim about the server answering today. Each row preserves its date, environment, previous run, ceiling, branch, verdict and exclusions. A faster candidate that fails its gate remains a failure.</p>"
