text smt250 "crates/site-builder/data/status.json"
text smt251 "Recorded project state"
text smt252 "<p>The canonical layer record was updated "
text smt253 "updated"
text smt254 ". These dated states preserve their original evidence scope; they are not an assertion that a past release or implementation note describes the current checkout. For the current product, use <a href=\"/alpha/\">the Alpha release page</a> and <a href=\"https://github.com/aien-dev/sovereign-intelligence/releases\">the release record</a>. <a href=\"/status.json\">status.json</a> and <a href=\"/llms.txt\">llms.txt</a> use this same canonical record.</p>"
text smt255 "story"
text smt256 "Not another app on someone else's computer"
text smt257 "<p>Most AI lives in a rented stack. A provider owns the machine, the model, the price, and the off switch. Your agent exists at their pleasure, forgets on their schedule, and works under their terms.</p><p>AienOS is the opposite bet: a sovereign machine, built from the first instruction after firmware upward, where a persistent intelligence lives on hardware you own. It keeps its memory, its identity, and its receipts on your side of the line. The hardware underneath is capability, not identity: machines can be replaced, and the lineage persists.</p></section>"
text smt258 "terminal"
text smt259 "The syscall interface, simulated"
text smt260 "<p class=\"badge\">INTERACTIVE SIMULATION</p><p>A simulation that runs entirely in your browser. No live machine is attached to this page, and nothing you type leaves it. It shows the shape of the interface the real machine speaks. The real machine's proof is in the evidence section, receipts and all.</p><div class=\"terminal-shell panel\"><p>AienOS REPL v0.4.0 (sm_121a · aarch64 · 128GB LPDDR5x) · COHERENT_ACTIVE</p><div class=\"cluster\"><button type=\"button\" data-cmd=\"sys_telemetry\">sys_telemetry</button><button type=\"button\" data-cmd=\"sys_alloc_kv\">sys_alloc_kv</button><button type=\"button\" data-cmd=\"sys_vault\">sys_vault</button><button type=\"button\" id=\"terminal-clear-btn\">[clear]</button></div><div id=\"terminal-output\" role=\"log\"><p class=\"terminal-log-line sys\">[*] AienOS Neural Kernel v0.4.0 initialized on GB10 (aarch64).</p><p class=\"terminal-log-line sys\">[*] Unified coherent address space: 128 GB LPDDR5x online.</p><p class=\"terminal-log-line sys\">[*] Capability vault sealed. Zero disk secrets invariant active.</p><p class=\"terminal-log-line sys\">[*] Type a syscall below or click one of the quick trigger buttons above.</p></div><form id=\"terminal-form\"><label for=\"terminal-input\">Simulated syscall</label><input id=\"terminal-input\" type=\"text\" placeholder=\"sys_telemetry, sys_alloc_kv, sys_vault, help\" autocomplete=\"off\"><button type=\"submit\">RUN</button></form></div></section><script defer src=\"/js/terminal.js\"></script>"
text smt261 "follow"
text smt262 "Follow the work."
text smt263 "<p>Watch the repositories, read the receipts, open an issue. Release artifacts and installation instructions are on <a href=\"/alpha/\">the Alpha page</a>; source, qualification and deployment are separate states.</p><p>Learning to code with AI? You are welcome here. <a href=\"/learn/\">Start with a practical working method</a>, then <a href=\"/hive/\">watch my agents and me in Hive</a>: the instructions, the models, the corrections, and the work as it happens.</p><div class=\"cluster\"><a href=\"https://github.com/aien-dev\">GitHub: aien-dev</a><a href=\"https://github.com/aien-dev/aien-sovereign-core\">AIEN core tree</a><a href=\"/now/\">Now: what is being done today</a><a href=\"/progress/\">Project progress</a></div><p id=\"follow-reach\">Want to reach me? <a href=\"https://x.com/mdrakestapleton\">Follow me on X, @mdrakestapleton</a>, email <a href=\"mailto:drake@aienos.com\">drake@aienos.com</a>, or read <a href=\"/contact/\">where I am and how to reach me</a>.</p><p>Machine-readable: <a href=\"/status.json\">status.json</a> · <a href=\"/facts.json\">facts.json</a> · <a href=\"/llms.txt\">llms.txt</a></p><a class=\"box-link source-link\" href=\"https://github.com/aien-dev\">The public repositories</a></section>"
text smt264 "Sovereign Intelligence™"
text smt265 "Sovereign Intelligence, built on AienOS. My work toward persistent intelligence that belongs to the person running it, from the language to the machine."
text smt266 "<div class=\"cluster\"><a class=\"button\" href=\"/alpha/\">Install / explore Alpha</a><a class=\"button button-secondary\" href=\"https://github.com/aien-dev/sovereign-intelligence/releases\">Releases and signatures</a><a href=\"https://x.com/mdrakestapleton\">Follow me on X</a></div><section class=\"section dashboard-grid\" aria-label=\"Explore the owned stack\"><article class=\"hub-card panel\"><h2>Your starting point</h2><p>Sovereign Intelligence (SI) is the product and stack index. Alpha is experimental, not a promise that every machine or feature is qualified. Read the release's exact scope before running it.</p><a href=\"/alpha/\">Installer, source and release evidence</a><a class=\"box-link\" href=\"https://github.com/aien-dev/sovereign-intelligence\">SI source and stack map</a></article><article class=\"hub-card panel\"><h2>The system and its kernel</h2><p>AienOS keeps its own identity. Aienux is the kernel, not a new name for the whole system.</p><a href=\"/machine/\">Hardware, evidence and the closed loop</a><a class=\"box-link\" href=\"https://github.com/aien-dev/AienOS-nv\">AienOS</a><a href=\"https://github.com/aien-dev/aienux\">Aienux kernel</a></article><article class=\"hub-card panel\"><h2>The language and the GPU</h2><p>Omega makes programs explicit. CUDA++ is its GPU half. The implementation, remaining dependencies and receipts are inspectable.</p><a href=\"/omega/\">Omega</a> · <a href=\"/cudaplusplus/\">CUDA++</a><a class=\"box-link\" href=\"https://github.com/aien-dev/omega-mv\">Omega source</a></article><article class=\"hub-card panel\"><h2>Learn, discover, meet Allen</h2><p>I share the working methods, the mistakes and the evidence so that people learning to build with AI can start from real work.</p><a href=\"/learn/\">Learn</a> · <a href=\"/discoveries/\">Discoveries</a> · <a href=\"/allen/\">Allen</a><a class=\"box-link\" href=\"https://github.com/aien-dev/allen\">Allen source</a></article></section>"
text smt267 "<details class=\"section\"><summary>The design, machines and full evidence record</summary>"
text smt268 "</details>"
